# Go CLI conventions

- Prefer existing packages under `cmd/terradrift` and `internal/`; do not add parallel frameworks.
- Fail closed on truncated adapter/policy I/O and size limits (`internal/ioutil` patterns).
- Policy is a **publish gate**: run before history/notify/artifacts persist; never invoke a shell implicitly for `--policy-command`.
- Attribute **paths** always; values paths-only unless `--attribute-values`; keep sensitive values redacted.
- External HTTP (webhooks, GitHub, artifacts): timeouts and SSRF-safe clients — see `SECURITY.md`.
- Deeper design: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Trust boundary: `SECURITY.md`.
